diff --git a/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/nss/ath11k/999-800-ath11k-Add-threaded-napi.patch b/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/nss/ath11k/999-800-ath11k-Add-threaded-napi.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..0f6cf557e923af40fe8a61642ff847c29885e26a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/nss/ath11k/999-800-ath11k-Add-threaded-napi.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,97 @@
+ath11k: run the NAPI contexts in threads
+
+dev_set_threaded() on the ath11k NAPI netdevs, plus a name for each so
+the threads are identifiable in ps.
+
+This is not a tuning preference. The CE interrupts must stay on cpu0 -
+the firmware asserts if they are spread - so without threaded NAPI the
+Wi-Fi receive processing runs in softirq context on cpu0, which is
+also the core the NSS firmware delivers host-terminated flows to
+through N2H queue 0. Threading the NAPI contexts is the only lever
+that moves that work off cpu0 without touching the CE affinity.
+
+Measured: under a Wi-Fi client to wired host transfer the busiest NAPI
+thread accumulated 75 jiffies of system time in a 20 second run and
+was last scheduled on core 2, with the rest spread over cores 1 to 3.
+None of it landed on cpu0.
+
+Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
+
+diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c
