+qualcommax: ipq8074: add the ipmr/ip6mr MFC offload hooks for ECM
+
+ECM accelerates routed multicast from the kernel's multicast forwarding
+cache. Let it register a callback for MFC entry changes, look up an
+entry's output interfaces and feed the offloaded packet counts back
+into the entry, for IPv4 and IPv6.
+
+Ported from qosmio/openwrt-ipq (0604-1-qca-add-mcs-support), keeping
+only the ipmr/ip6mr part; ECM reads the bridge ports from the bridge's
+own multicast database.
+
+Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
+--- a/include/linux/mroute.h
++++ b/include/linux/mroute.h
+@@ -92,4 +92,44 @@ struct rtmsg;
+ int ipmr_get_route(struct net *net, struct sk_buff *skb,
+ 		   __be32 saddr, __be32 daddr,
+ 		   struct rtmsg *rtm, u32 portid);
++
++/* QCA ECM multicast offload - Start */
++#define IPMR_MFC_EVENT_UPDATE   1
++#define IPMR_MFC_EVENT_DELETE   2
